{
  "case_id": "2007-06-179",
  "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ALLISON M. ZIEVE, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nTHEODORE B. OLSON, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent.\nEDWIN S. KNEEDLER, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What if the manufacturer wants to make what you call an improvement? Can it simply market the product with that improvement without further FDA action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, before that decision is reached, let me ask you this -- under State law, either generally or specifically under the law of the State that you are trying to invoke here, does the jury -- does the finder of fact weigh the potential risks of injury and illness against the probable benefits to the health of the patient?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought that was something a little different than that. The question that I have which might be helpful to me, if you can answer it, is -- that's being serious about it -- I'd be helped by knowing what the specific design defect is that you claim? That is, in what respect was this catheter -- and I'd like you to refer to the details of the catheter -- in what respect, what material or what shape or what -- what it is about this catheter that you as the plaintiff think was designed defectively, if you can tell me?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Zieve",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The labeling claim is that the label was -- inadequately warned or was misleading because although at one place it lists among 12 precautions not to inflate the balloon above the rate of burst pressure, which was eight, at another place it says to -- it has a chart that shows inflation up to 13 atmosphere, and at another place in the instructions, it says inflate to the nominal pressure, which is --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "21 CFR 814.39(d)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The principal difference is this preemption provision that is the fundamental issue in this case. Section 360k(a)(1), that similar provision was not put by Congress in the new drug --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that was a slightly different point than Justice Kennedy's one; what was -- if it is the same point, I agree with you, that there is an elaborate process of information exchange from the manufacturer and from doctors and from all over with respect to these medical devices."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Olson, the other side says well, you know, these are all horribles but, in fact, we have had tort suits and manufacturers haven't taken their products off the market."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF EDWIN S. KNEEDLER, ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "State legislatures or State regulatory agencies could adopt laws or regulations that would direct the manufacturer to manufacture or design the product or to give labeling that would conflict with what the FDA had just approved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose a label is approved in a very specific form under PMA, and then a year later, it turns out, unforeseen by anyone, that doctors are just -- many good doctors are just reading it the wrong way and it's dangerous."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-179",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5db4516f2ccd18a8c0e0fe2f29acb7926d16bb77ddef46012dbef2ca3044db60",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5db4516f2ccd-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:11 a.m. , the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
